  </data>
  <data name="HP_DashboardDescription1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Displays today's summary and the calendar of appointments. By double-tapping a doctor's name in the calendar, you can view their appointments for the day on the right side. Each appointment can be updated with one of the following statuses:</value>
    <comment>HP_DashboardDescription1</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DashboardStatusAttending.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Attending – The patient is currently with the doctor.</value>
    <comment>HP_DashboardStatusAttending.Text</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DashboardStatusAttended.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Attended – The patient has already seen the doctor and left.</value>
    <comment>HP_DashboardStatusAttended</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DashboardStatusMissed.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Missed – The patient did not come to the clinic.</value>
    <comment>HP_DashboardStatusMissed</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DoctorsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Doctors</value>
    <comment>HP_DoctorsTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DoctorsDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Add, edit, deactivate, or clear doctor profiles. You can use the following shortcuts: Add (F1), Edit (F2), Deactivate (F3), or Clear all data with Clear (F4).</value>
    <comment>HP_DoctorsDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DoctorsWarning.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Important: The field marked with a red circle is mandatory. Notifications may not work properly if this field is left empty, even if no validation warning appears.</value>
    <comment>HP_DoctorsWarning</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_PatientsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Patients</value>
    <comment>HP_PatientsTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_PatientsDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Manage patient records and view visit history. You can use the following shortcuts: Add (F1), Edit (F2), Deactivate (F3), or Clear all data with Clear (F4).</value>
    <comment>HP_PatientsDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_PatientsWarning.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Important: The field marked with a red circle is mandatory. Notifications may not work properly if this field is left empty, even if no validation warning appears.</value>
    <comment>HP_PatientsWarning</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_AppointmentsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Appointments</value>
    <comment>HP_AppointmentsTitle.Text</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_AppointmentsDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Schedule and control upcoming visits. You can use the following shortcuts: Add (F1), Edit (F2), Deactivate (F3), or Clear all data with Clear (F4).</value>
    <comment>HP_AppointmentsDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_AppointmentsSearch.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When adding a patient to an appointment, you can search using multiple fields: first name, middle name, last name, or full name; patient ID; patient code (e.g., PT000001); email address; mobile phone number; age (e.g., 35, 45...); or date of birth (in dd/MM/yyyy format, e.g., 01/01/2000).</value>
    <comment>HP_AppointmentsSearch</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_AppointmentsAdd.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>After searching, you can double-click (or tap) on the patient’s name to quickly add a new appointment.</value>
    <comment>HP_AppointmentsAdd</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_ReportsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Reports</value>
    <comment>HP_ReportsTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_ReportsDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>View visit statistics and performance summaries. Reports provide detailed counts and insights for:</value>
    <comment>HP_ReportsDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_ReportsTotalDoctors.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Total doctors – statistics available for today, this week, this month, and this year.</value>
    <comment>HP_ReportsTotalDoctors</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_ReportsTotalPatients.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Total patients – statistics available for today, this week, this month, and this year.</value>
    <comment>HP_ReportsTotalPatients</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_ReportsMissedAppointments.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Missed appointments – statistics available for today, this week, this month, and this year.</value>
    <comment>HP_ReportsMissedAppointments</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_ReportsInsights.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>These reports help track clinic performance, identify trends, and ensure better planning for resources.</value>
    <comment>HP_ReportsInsights</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_UsersTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Users</value>
    <comment>HP_UsersTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_UsersDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Users section contains two main pages: User Management and User Roles.</value>
    <comment>HP_UsersDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_UserManagement.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• User Management – Add new users, update existing ones, deactivate accounts, or clear all data. Shortcuts: Add (F1), Update (F2), Deactivate (F3), Clear (F4).</value>
    <comment>HP_UserManagement</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_UserRoles.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• User Roles – Manage predefined roles and permissions. We recommend keeping the default roles unchanged for stability. Shortcuts: Add (F1), Update (F2), Deactivate (F3), Clear (F4).</value>
    <comment>HP_UserRoles</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DefaultAccountsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Default Accounts:</value>
    <comment>HP_DefaultAccountsTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DefaultAdmin.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Admin – Username: admin, Password: admin1234</value>
    <comment>HP_DefaultAdmin</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DefaultUser.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• User – Username: user, Password: user1234</value>
    <comment>HP_DefaultUser</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_DefaultWarning.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>⚠️ For security, please change these default passwords immediately after first login.</value>
    <comment>HP_DefaultWarning</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Settings</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Settings section allows you to configure and personalize LiteClinic. Available options include:</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsThemes.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Change themes – Switch between available visual themes to customize the look and feel.</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsThemes</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsNotifications.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Manage notifications – Adjust notification preferences to control how alerts are delivered.</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsNotifications</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsTelegram.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Configure Telegram bot – Set up and manage the Telegram bot for appointment notifications.</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsTelegram</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsBackup.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Backup database – Save your clinic data securely in a safe location for recovery purposes.</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsBackup</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_SettingsLogs.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Open log files – Access diagnostic logs to help identify issues. These logs can be shared with support if you encounter problems.</value>
    <comment>HP_SettingsLogs</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_AboutTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• About</value>
    <comment>HP_AboutTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_AboutDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Learn more about LiteClinic, its version details, and review the terms of use.</value>
    <comment>HP_AboutDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_LogoutTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• Logout</value>
    <comment>HP_LogoutTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_LogoutDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exit the application securely. Logging out ensures that your session is closed properly and prevents unauthorized access to clinic data.</value>
    <comment>HP_LogoutDescription</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_TroubleshootingTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Troubleshooting</value>
    <comment>HP_TroubleshootingTitle</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_TroubleshootingInternet.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If notifications don’t appear, check your internet connection and Windows notification settings.</value>
    <comment>HP_TroubleshootingInternet</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_TroubleshootingDoctors.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ensure that doctors and patients are correctly added and not deactivated.</value>
    <comment>HP_TroubleshootingDoctors</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_TroubleshootingAppointments.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Verify that appointment dates and times are entered correctly.</value>
    <comment>HP_TroubleshootingAppointments</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="HP_TroubleshootingTelegram.Text" xml:space="preserve">
