  <data name="MiP_TelegramTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Telegram Bot Integration</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramIntro.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Follow these steps to create a Telegram bot and connect it to your account. This will allow the app to send you notifications directly in Telegram.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 1: Open BotFather in Telegram and start a chat.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 2: Send /newbot and follow prompts to create a bot.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 3: Copy the API token provided by BotFather.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 4: Start your bot, send a message, then call getUpdates to find your chat ID.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep5.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 5: Test sending a message using sendMessage with your token and chat ID.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep6.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 6: Add the token and chat ID into the app settings to enable notifications.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep7.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 7: Use the following custom commands to register users with the bot.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramCmdAdmin.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• /admin – Assigns the admin role to the bot creator (usually the owner).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramCmdDoctor.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• /doctor – Retrieves the doctor ID from the TelegramLog file in the Logs folder.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramCmdStart.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>• /start – Retrieves the patient ID from the same TelegramLog file.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramBotToken.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bot token (required)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramBotToken.ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enter your Telegram bot token to connect the application with your bot.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramBotDisplayName.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bot display name (optional)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramBotDisplayName.ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Provide a friendly name for your bot. This is shown to patients for easier recognition.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramAdminChatId.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Admin Chat ID (optional)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramAdminChatId.ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
