  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 8: Add custom commands to your bot using BotFather.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8Intro.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you want your bot to recognize /admin, /doctor, and /start, you must register them in BotFather:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8_1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Open Telegram and start a chat with BotFather.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8_2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. Type /mybots and select your bot.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8_3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. Choose 'Edit Bot' → 'Edit Commands'.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8_4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>4. Enter the commands you want, one per line, with a short description:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramCmdAdminDesc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>/admin - Assigns admin role (creator only)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramCmdDoctorDesc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>/doctor - Retrieves doctor ID from TelegramLog file</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramCmdStartDesc.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>/start - Default command for patients to register ID, also can be retrieved from TelegramLog file</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramStep8_5.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>5. Save changes. Now your bot will officially recognize these commands.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MiP_TelegramReminder.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>⚠️ Reminder: Each user (admin, doctor, patient) can use these commands only once per day to avoid flooding. The bot will not respond to other questions or any kind of message outside these commands.</value>
  </data>
